I'm doing nethack again.  This time I thought I would try a knight.

I got several characters killed so far.  My current one started on a
bad note:  a few turns into the game a rock fell on my pony and he
died!  I've almost been killed several times - I have to get better AC
soon.
It is only -1.

Anyway, my main point is that nethack is still interesting even though
I've "won" the game before.  I've read enough spoilers and played
enough to ascend a character, but I still run into fun new things when
I play.

I thought a knight would be fun because it could ride things and jump.
 But other little things are fun.  I haven't played a lawful character
before so I've never seen that sacrifices disappear in a flash of
light instead of bursting into flames.  I think what makes nethack fun
is all the details.

Also, I'm playing under CYGWIN instead of the DOS version so I got
this funny "Core dumped." message when I ate an apple.  I admit I
scrambled around for a few minutes looking to see if anything was
wrong before realizing it was a joke.

Anyway, I've got a new pony.  I've got Excalibur.  I'm tenth level. 
I'm working my way up Sokoban and have almost cleared the mines.  I
hope to eventually do a twoweapon character this time.  I'd also like
to see if I can do some spells once I get rid of the metal armor.  But
I have a long way to go.

